{
  "notes": [
    "Biomes for Generate Map's ground locations (Colony, Outpost, Small City, Ruins, Wilderness, Cave). Ships and stations have no biome.",
    "The list draws on the Captain's Log Solo RPG (beast Preferred Environment table: deciduous forest, swamps, standing water, sandy and rocky desert, arctic, volcanic features; Primary World classes H desert, P glaciated, D barren). Everything here is prototype content: tiles, features, densities and building styles are not from the book.",
    "ground / path: open ground and the paths and trails laid on it. trail: Wilderness only, a track across the map (null = none). plants: what grows at a colony's edges, around an outpost, in ruins and in a city's plaza. boulder: loose rocks outside. fence: yard fences at a colony (null = no fences, because the fence art is drawn on temperate ground).",
    "walls.prefab: colony and outpost buildings. walls.city: Small City buildings. cave: floor, wall and boulder tiles for caves.",
    "features run in order on open ground. blob: patches grown from random spots (tiles: one picked per patch), one per `per` tiles of map area, `size` tiles each. scatter: single tiles, one per `per` tiles. line: wandering lines edge to edge, one per `per` tiles (at least one), with extra `crossings`. fringe: `tile` beside every `around` tile with probability `chance`. Solid features never cut the walkable map in two.",
    "Wilderness uses the full feature density; settlements use less (see featureScale in mapGenerators.js). caveFeatures: the same kinds, on cave floor.",
    "world: 'earth' or 'alien', the group the editor's Biome list shows it under. Jungle, Grassland, Tundra, Coast, Mountains, Geothermal Field and the alien biomes after Barren are prototype additions with no source-book basis.",
    "card: colours for Generate Card's drawn episode pictures (src/maps/cardArt.js). skies: the skies it may pick (day, dusk, night, overcast, murky, desertDay, pale, volcanic, airless, alienViolet, alienTeal, toxic, rust). ground: far, middle and near hill colours. plant: tree, pine, mangrove, cactus, iceSpike, rock, crater, jungleTree, acacia, shrub, palm, crystal, mushroom, bulb, glowTree or geyser. rock: cave and cliff colour. building: settlement wall colour. extra: water, sea, acid, sulphur, lava, crevasse or null. mountains: the chance (0-1) of a mountain range on the horizon, instead of the location's default."
  ],
